<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Ottoman Tripolitania</h1><p class="st-meta">1551 CE – 1711 CE · capital Tripoli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Tripoli as an Ottoman province and corsair base, ruled by pashas and then deys until the Karamanli dynasty took power in 1711.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ottoman fleet captured <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-tripoli">Tripoli</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> in 1551. The corsair <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turgut-reis">Turgut Reis</a>, who had helped take the city, became its governor in 1553 and extended Ottoman authority along the coast and inland, making <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tripolitania">Tripolitania</a> a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Pashas sent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> shared power with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> officers and, from the early 17th century, deys chosen by the garrison. Corsairing in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and the trans-Saharan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> sustained the treasury, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-fezzan">Sultanate of Fezzan</a> paid tribute. Dey Mehmed Saqizli extended control over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> in the 1630s and 1640s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Chronic coups between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissaries</a> and pashas ended in 1711, when the cavalry officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-karamanli">Ahmed Karamanli</a> seized power, killed the Ottoman officials and founded a hereditary dynasty, beginning <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/karamanli-tripoli">Karamanli Tripoli</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ottoman-tripolitania.jpg" alt="Ottoman Tripolitania" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Bamse · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maritime_flag_of_Regency_of_Tripoli_(18th_century).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1551 CE – 1711 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tripoli</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Turgut Reis, Mehmed Saqizli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Ottoman Turkish, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Libya</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Eyalet of Tripoli, Regency of Tripoli</dd></dl></aside></div>
